From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:21:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: stop the Q25 keyboard driver logging every key and
 trackpad move

bbqX0kbd builds with DEBUG_LEVEL FE|RW|LD, so BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_LOG prints
several pr_err lines per interrupt, key press and trackpad movement. Send
them to pr_debug instead: they compile out on GKI builds without dynamic
debug for this module, and BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_ERR still reports errors.
---
 drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd/debug_levels.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd/debug_levels.h b/drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd/debug_levels.h
index cd8b7b43..a6c20680 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd/debug_levels.h
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd/debug_levels.h
@@ -33,7 +33,13 @@
 #define DRIVER_NAME			"BBQX0KBD"
  
 #if DEBUG_LEVEL
-#define BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_LOG(fmt, args...)    pr_err("[%s] %s %d: " fmt, DRIVER_NAME, __func__, __LINE__, ##args)
+/*
+ * SableOS: the trace lines below run on every interrupt, key and trackpad
+ * movement. At pr_err they reach the console and logd's kernel reader each
+ * time; at pr_debug they compile out unless DEBUG or dynamic debug is on.
+ * Real errors still use BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_ERR.
+ */
+#define BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_LOG(fmt, args...)    pr_debug("[%s] %s %d: " fmt, DRIVER_NAME, __func__, __LINE__, ##args)
 #else
 #define BBQX0KBD_KEYBOARD_LOG(fmt, args...)
 #endif
